Z||000000||86SE||06-27-2000||02:12 PM||||Whitch is best for the Fiero, besides Premium Unleaded?  Ethonol claims it is good for your car, but its octane level is mid-ranged.  <P>What are their octane levels?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||06-27-2000||04:04 PM||||Stock Fieros run great on 87 octane.  Using the high test unnecessarily adds unneeded profits to the oil companies.(0.20 cents more per gallon)<P>This is for stock engines that are tuned up.<P>If you add HP chips or have adjusted timing, or have a modified engine, then you may need 93 octane for proper operation.<P>Ethanol is an oxygen additive to gasoline which is supposed to lower tail pipe emissions, making it a cleaner burning fuel.<P>Some area of dense population (Chicago, Milwalkee) with poor air quality are required by the EPA to have these fuels burned in these area to help air quality and to help the corn farmers sell corn to make ethanol.  You could be sitting drinking the ethanol and get a real buzz, but your feeding it to your Fiero. <P>I think most all the race cars are using ethanol (alcohol) fuels in there cars today.  I can get racing fuel here (103 octane) for $3.499 a gallon, or 87 octane for $1.639.  For a daily driver an addition $166 a gallon is not necessary.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sillhouette.com||06-27-2000||06:37 PM||||I've tried 100 low lead from airplanes that runs pretty good if you don't have a cat and the interesting fuel is 130 from airplanes again that was quite the difference.  Too bad they don't refine 130 anymore all that is left for airplanes is the 100 low lead.  <P>Cheers||||reg||1
Z||000003||frontal lobe||06-27-2000||07:09 PM||||86SE, don't bother with ethanol.  It doesn't do anything better for your car.  It runs fine but no better than REAL gasoline, but it gets WORSE gas mileage.  The completely trustworthy EPA admits to 3% worse, but it's really 5 to 7% worse.  So you are paying 5 to 7% MORE for the ethanol gasoline vs. REAL gasoline.  I happen to live in the Milwaukee area and we have to use the stupid reformulated junk.  At least it's down to the BARGAIN price of 1.85 a gallon but then when you factor the 7% mileage penalty it's really 1.98 compared to REAL gasoline.  And Milwaukee wouldn't even HAVE to use reformulated gas if all CHICAGO's pollution didn't blow up here.  SOMEBODY HOSE ME DOWN, I'M GOING TO SPONTANEOUSLY COMBUST.  OK.  I'm better now.<P>Summary, ethanol isn't an advantage.||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||06-27-2000||09:57 PM||||Ethanol isnt supposed to be very good for your fuel pump,and injectors either.<BR>BTW,AV(iation) gas is a different molecular weight than automotive gas,will make your car run lean if I remember,which is ok if you're rich to begin with,however...<BR>Oh,another thing,I used to use this cheap gas from AM/PM that was part(mostly)ethanol,and my 4 cylinder Fiero hated it.<BR>I try and stick with Chevron,or Texaco now,unless I'm stuck in Detroit,like now,where I use Sunoco.<p>[This message has been edited by lowCG (edited 06-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||fldevel||06-28-2000||08:06 PM|||| well to tell you the truth my 85 GT V6 dosent run much different on high octain the it does regular ..well maby it picks the front wheels up of the ground an extra inch r two on hard takeoffs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  ||||reg||1
